## Naming quick-ref (Effective Dart)

| Kind             | Convention              | Example                          |
|------------------|-------------------------|----------------------------------|
| Types            | `UpperCamelCase`        | `LoginBloc`, `UserModel`         |
| Files / dirs     | `snake_case`            | `login_bloc.dart`                |
| Members / locals | `lowerCamelCase`        | `onSubmit`, `isLoading`          |
| `static const`   | `lowerCamelCase`        | `defaultTimeout`                 |
| Events           | imperative / past-tense | `LoginSubmitted`, `FetchStarted` |

## Feature folder quick-ref

```
lib/features/{feature}/
  presentation/
    view/          ← screen widgets, BlocProvider wiring
    widgets/       ← dumb UI widgets
    bloc/          ← *_bloc.dart, *_event.dart, *_state.dart
  data/            ← repository impl, DTOs, API mapping
  domain/          ← repository interfaces, pure helpers (optional)
```

Shared: `lib/widgets/` · `lib/data/models/` · `lib/core/`
Routing: `lib/core/routing/` (`route_names.dart`, `app_routes.dart`, `app_router.dart`)

## Formatting quick-ref

- Run `dart format` before every commit
- Prefer `~80` char lines
- Import order: `dart:` → `package:` → relative (each group sorted)
- Prefer `final`; annotate return types; no `dynamic` on public APIs
- Use `isEmpty` / `isNotEmpty`; use `async` / `await`
- Dates shown in UI: `MM/dd/yyyy` via `formatDateMmDdYyyy` in `lib/core/utils/date_formatters.dart`
